11. Explain the Library solution.

→ TODO #1: For every author, filter books using authorId and store the result in the authorsBooks map.

→ TODO #2: Use flatMap() to combine all authors' book lists into one stream, then filter by BookType.

→ TODO #3: Use the size of each author's book list to update booksAmount.

→ Time complexity: Assigning books is O(A × B), where A is the number of authors and B is the number of books. Retrieving books by type is O(B) overall, assuming the map contains all books.

→ Note: The solution assumes each author's ID is unique and every book has a valid author ID.

